-- ----- fragment: minion_psalms_119.sql (Psalm 119) -----
-- Chapter: Psalm 119 — THE GREAT TORAH ACROSTIC (176 verses, 22 stanzas aleph→tav), the longest chapter
-- in Scripture and the ANTI-ANTINOMIAN CAPSTONE of the whole framework. Nearly every verse exalts the
-- Torah under its EIGHT-FOLD ARCHITECTURE of synonyms: (1) LAW (torah, v.1,18,29,34,44,51,53,55,61,70,
-- 72,77,85,92,97,109,113,126,136,142,150,153,163,165,174), (2) TESTIMONIES (v.2,14,22,24,31,36,46,59,79,
-- 88,95,99,111,119,125,129,138,144,146,152,157,167,168), (3) PRECEPTS (v.4,15,27,40,45,56,63,69,78,87,93,
-- 94,100,104,110,128,134,141,159,168,173), (4) STATUTES (v.5,8,12,16,23,26,33,48,54,64,68,71,80,83,112,117,
-- 118,124,135,145,155,171), (5) COMMANDMENTS (v.6,10,19,21,32,35,47,48,60,66,73,86,96,98,115,127,131,143,
-- 151,166,172,176), (6) JUDGMENTS (v.7,13,20,30,39,43,52,62,75,84,102,106,108,120,121,137,149,156,160,164,
-- 175), (7) WORD/DAVAR (v.9,11,16,17,25,28,42,43,49,57,65,74,81,82,89,101,105,107,114,130,139,147,148,160,
-- 161,162,169,170,172), (8) WAY/WAYS (v.1,3,5,14,15,26,27,29,30,32,33,37,59,168). The whole acrostic is one
-- man's confession that the Torah is the living covenant delight written on the heart — NEVER a defunct
-- "old covenant." 1 John 2:3-4 is the filter at its absolute peak: to know Him is to keep His commandments.
-- Because of the 176 verses we curate framework-bearing THEMATIC threads (not per-verse), each gathering
-- the load-bearing verses of that theme across the stanzas.
-- Tag: ps119   Temp view: _s302_ps119_lookup
-- Sort band: base 24950, step 3 -> threads at 24950,24953,24956,24959,24962,24965,24968,24971,24974,24977,
--   24980,24983 (12 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','psalms',119,v
-- ⚠ SLUG PREFIX IS SINGULAR: psalm-119-... (verified 0 hits in EXISTING_SLUGS.txt)
--
-- Psalm 119 coverage (by theme-block; "none warranted" recorded where chosen):
--   vv.1-3 (Blessed are the undefiled in the way, who walk in the law... blessed are they that keep his testimonies)
--        NT:     ★ Matthew 5:6 (hunger and thirst after righteousness); ★ 1 John 2:3 (the filter) — THREAD 1
--        Extras: none warranted        Tanakh: ★ Psalm 1:1-2 (delight in the law); ★ Deuteronomy 28:1 (hearken... do all his commandments) — THREAD 1
--   vv.9-11 (Wherewithal shall a young man cleanse his way? ...Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin)
--        NT:     ★ Matthew 4:4 (man shall live by every word) — THREAD 2
--        Extras: none warranted        Tanakh: ★★ Deuteronomy 6:6 (these words shall be in thine heart); ★ Jeremiah 15:16 (thy words were found, and I did eat them) — THREAD 2
--   v.18 + v.130 (Open thou mine eyes, that I may behold wondrous things out of thy law / The entrance of thy words giveth light)
--        NT:     ★★ Luke 24:45 (then opened he their understanding); ★★ 2 Corinthians 3:14-16 (the VAIL done away — not the law); ★ 1 Corinthians 2:14 — THREAD 3
--        Extras: none warranted        Tanakh: (Torah-light held to THREAD 8)
--   v.32 + v.34,v.36 (I will run the way of thy commandments, when thou shalt enlarge my heart / Incline my heart unto thy testimonies)
--        NT:     ★★★ none-NT-only — fused with the new-covenant prophets; 2 Corinthians 3:3 (written in fleshy tables of the heart) — THREAD 4 KEYSTONE
--        Extras: ★ Sirach 24:23 (the book of the covenant... the law which Moses commanded) — THREAD 4
--        Tanakh: ★★★ Jeremiah 31:33 (I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts); ★★ Ezekiel 36:26-27 (a new heart... cause you to walk in my statutes) — THREAD 4
